## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are current product/platform authority. Existing domain-specific safety rules in this file remain valid.

Messenger/native roadmap does not alter current payment-provider trust boundaries. Platform shells must call the same authoritative payment/billing APIs unless a future native-store payment issue explicitly designs another compliant provider flow.


# Payment rules

- Never grant subscription/top-up because browser says payment succeeded.
- Server resolves plan/price/amount; client cannot set authoritative price/provider budget/payment status/userId.
- Real grant occurs only after verified provider event/webhook and idempotent DB transaction.
- Verify webhook signatures/timestamps/replay protections according to provider documentation.
- `(provider, providerEventId)` and provider payment identity are unique where appropriate.
- Duplicate concurrent webhooks produce one state transition/grant.
- Mock payment routes/providers are local/test only and must not be registered in staging/production.
- Refunds use explicit state + compensating accounting; do not mutate historical ledger entries.
- Normalize provider errors; do not expose payment provider internals/secrets.
- Payment/admin adjustment actions require audit events.
